{"availability":"available","full":"CemBeast/Taskboard-Lite","name":"Taskboard-Lite","description":"Very simple to do task management for my learning of Web Dev","category":"Education","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-10-15T19:44:03Z","updated":"2026-01-31T03:42:30Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://cembeast.github.io/Taskboard-Lite/**","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:45.950Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:45.950Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:45.950Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:22:45.950Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["askBoard is a web-based Kanban app that bakes automation into everyday task management using a small team of coordinating software agents. Instead of forcing users to manually create and maintain tasks, the system parses natural-language input into structured tasks, auto-prioritizes based on urgency, issues reminders ahead of deadlines, and generates weekly progress summaries—coordinated by a central backend “Coordinator.” ￼","Problem. Students and small teams often lose time and momentum to manual task entry, triage, and follow-ups—resulting in missed deadlines and scattered focus. Existing Kanban tools are either too manual or too heavy to extend. ￼","Solution & Success Vision. Deliver a functional React + Node app where agents collaborate: typing “Finish project draft by Friday” creates a prioritized task; near-due items trigger reminders; and weekly reports summarize done vs. pending. An MVP ships with a clean, responsive UI, stable Node/Express backend, JSON persistence (with a path to Mongo/Postgres), and well-documented agent modules. ￼"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CemBeast/Taskboard-Lite/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fa204caec94a594193e4ef97794a36e682bbbe4f51d0c7e00de05ca97fc85167","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:46.064Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-1